# D53 / D10 message pin — the SOURCE is a field sub-place (`s.lock`), so the
# remedy must NOT name `^`: D10 rejects a bare `^` on a field/index sub-place
# as E_PartialMove, and `^s` would move a different value. The only followable
# remedy is wrapping the sub-place.
# CELL: lock=Mutex · position=push · source=field sub-place (shape=FieldIndex).
# Cross-lane pin: Rust gg has rendered the reconciled text since D10 landed;
# the SELF-HOST rendered the stale whole-shape "write `^s` to move" until this
# round. Both lanes must now render the sub-place arm.
# ggdef: ABSTAIN (Mutex out of subset; owner: ggdef stays simple).

struct Holder:
    Mutex[int] lock

void main():
    Holder s = Holder(Mutex[int](1))
    Vector[Mutex[int]] v = []
    v.push(s.lock)
    print(v.len())
